# Changes in 2.0.0:
#  - HIERARCHICAL RIG, still a single armature:
#        GLOBAL_MASTER  (master bone, root of everything)
#          +-- MASSIVE_ROOT  (parent bone of the top word)
#          |     +-- M_BONE, A_BONE, S1_BONE, S2_BONE, I_BONE, V_BONE, E_BONE
#          +-- WIN_ROOT  (parent bone of the bottom word)
#                +-- W_BONE, I2_BONE, N_BONE
#    The first word of a rig name is laid out on the TOP row, the second
#    word on the row BELOW it. Every letter keeps its own single bone.
#  - ORGANIC MOTION: the pure sine / uniform stagger look is gone. A loop-safe
#    "organic" wave (a sum of integer harmonics with random per-letter phases
#    and amplitudes, windowed by a sine envelope) replaces the mathematical
#    idle loops, staggers are jittered, and the two word-root bones carry
#    group-level motion, so letters move as families instead of metronomes.
#  - Clip layout is unchanged for all 12 variations:
#        ENTRY  1..30    LOOP 31..85    EXIT 86..100
#    Frames 30 / 31 / 85 / 86 still hold the identical rest pose on every
#    channel of every bone (master, word roots and letters).
#  - Everything else that 1.3.0 guaranteed is kept: exact axis conversion,
#    safe action replacement, direct F-Curve writing, verification.

